description:
`Temperature{ 98.6 }` does not say whether that is Celsius, Fahrenheit or Kelvin. A **static factory function** gives each way of building the object a name.

Write a class `Temperature` that stores Kelvin internally and has:

- a **private** constructor, so the only way to make one is through the factories;
- `static Temperature fromCelsius(double c)` (kelvin = c + 273.15);
- `static Temperature fromFahrenheit(double f)` (kelvin = (f − 32) × 5 / 9 + 273.15);
- `double kelvin() const`, `double celsius() const`, `double fahrenheit() const`.

